v 3
d 'EASI': module to estimate the Exact Affine Stone Index demand system
d
d  easi estimates the Exact Affine Stone Index (EASI) implicit Marshallian
d  demand system of Lewbel and Pendakur (2009) within Stata and Mata, by
d  iterated linear three-stage least squares with Slutsky symmetry imposed.
d  It reports expenditure, compensated and uncompensated price, and
d  demographic elasticities for the households, the individuals or the
d  market, with standard errors from the influence functions of the whole
d  procedure; sampling weights, robust, cluster and survey-design (svyset)
d  variance, and a design bootstrap. The households that do not buy some
d  goods are handled by imputing their missing prices (pimpute) and by the
d  Shonkwiler-Yen correction for censoring (selection), both carried into the
d  standard errors. easidiag diagnoses the data before estimation; predict
d  and estat engel give the Engel curves; tables with significance stars can
d  be written to Word, LaTeX, Excel, CSV or Markdown; a dialog box and help
d  examples run from clickable links are included. sr_easi is kept as a
d  backward-compatible wrapper. A technical note documents the model, the
d  estimator and the validation of the standard errors; it is included as an
d  ancillary file (easi_technical_note.pdf) and on Zenodo:
d  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22914058
d
d KW: demand system
d KW: EASI
d KW: Exact Affine Stone Index
d KW: price elasticities
d KW: household survey
d KW: censoring
d KW: survey design
d KW: three-stage least squares
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260930
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: email aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
d (A copy of the package as submitted to the SSC archive, version 2.0.1, to
d test it before SSC publishes it: the example data, the tours and the
d technical note are ancillary files, copied to the current folder by net get.)
d
